4,Relaxing Austronesian Music for the Soul | AYA • Amihan ...Welaun language - WikipediaReintroducing Welaun - JSTOR(PDF) Reintroducing Welaun - Academia.eduWelaun language - WikiwandStream euraxx | Listen to Austronesian traditional music ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jf5V5WCWUK4,"🌿 AYA – Amihan (Official Audio)🏝️ Isla Ancients presents a new artist.After the peaceful instrumental world of Kutalapu, Isla Ancients proudly introduces A... Welaun (also known as Bekais or Wekais) is an Austronesian language spoken on the border of East Timor and West Timor (a part of Indonesia). It is closely related to Tetun. Welaun is an Austronesian language of central Timor, straddling the border between Timor-Leste and the Indonesian regency of Belu. Welaun has been described by Hull (2003) and a 189 page Welaun–Tetun dictionary written by a native speaker has been published (da Silva 2012). In this article I provide an overview of Welaun, an Austronesian language of central Timor. Despite previous documentation, Welaun is mostly unknown to the scientific community. Welaun (also known as Bekais or Wekais) is an Austronesian language spoken on the border of East Timor and West Timor (a part of Indonesia). It is closely related to Tetun. Listen to Austronesian traditional music, a playlist curated by euraxx on desktop and mobile.",Welaun,Austronesian
